summary:
  Any media session on the receiver counts as the stream having been taken,
  so a television busy with something else reads as casting.

history:
  The verdict read pychromecast's session event, and any session sets it.
  A television in the middle of a YouTube programme was sent a station on
  2026-11-11: the helper said OK after 420 ms and YouTube played on, with
  the footer reading "Casting to" over it. The status names what a session
  holds, and the receiver hands the address back as it was given, so the
  helper asks for a session that holds the stream it sent. This mutant
  takes the content out of the question again.

target:
  package/contents/ui/cast.py

find:
      return (bool(url)
              and getattr(status, "media_session_id", None) is not None
              and getattr(status, "content_id", None) == url)

replace:
      return (bool(url)
              and getattr(status, "media_session_id", None) is not None)

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_cast_play.py::test_a_device_busy_with_something_else_is_not_casting.
